# Template for client/ToBe/.env — copy to `.env` only if you need to override
# the default. Local development works with no .env file at all.
#
# WARNING: everything here ships to the browser. Vite inlines every
# VITE_-prefixed variable into the built JavaScript, so anything placed in
# this file is publicly readable by anyone who loads the site. Never put a
# secret here — API keys and passwords belong in server/.env, which is never
# sent to the client.

# Origin of the API server. Defaults to http://localhost:5000 when unset,
# which is what local development uses.
#
# Two things to get right when deploying:
#   1. This is read at BUILD time, not runtime — set it before `npm run build`.
#      Changing it on the host afterwards does nothing until you rebuild.
#   2. It must pair with the server's CLIENT_ORIGIN. The auth cookie is
#      SameSite=Lax and CORS runs with credentials, so localhost and
#      127.0.0.1 are not interchangeable — mismatching them breaks login
#      while leaving every public page working, which makes it easy to miss.
#
# A trailing slash is stripped automatically (see src/apiConfig.js).
VITE_API_URL=
